factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 7 problems
  The reel_script and caption say the lorry driver braked suddenly and the bike hit the lorry's 'பின்னோக்கு' (rear part), which is an unusual phrasing; the article says the bike hit the lorry from behind, so the wording is ungrammatical/unclear as rendered.
  The reel_script says the siblings were 'going to Chennai for work' (சென்னை வேலைக்கு செல்லும் வழியில்), but the article says they were returning from Diwali holiday to Chennai, where they worked; the reason for travel is not accurately stated.
  The article says the siblings started from their village on a Pulsar bike to Chennai after Diwali leave; the draft omits that they were returning after Diwali holiday.
  The slides_spec says the siblings were 'இளைஞர்கள்' (youths) in the headline and 'பாதிக்கப்பட்டவர்கள' with a typo; the slide headline 'ஆணையம்பட்டி இளைஞர்கள் விபத்தில்' is acceptable but the caption/reel say the victims were sisters and brother, mixing descriptions.
  The slide 'போலீஸ் நடவடிக்கை' lists 'லாரி டிரைவர் திடீரென பிரேக் போட்டார்' as police action, mixing two different facts (police case registration and the cause of the accident) in one slide.
  The caption's 'நடவடிக்கை' line and the 'மக்கள் கவனத்திற்கு' advice (keep a safe distance behind lorries) is an invented advisory not stated in the article.
  The caption's English line 'Salem siblings die in bike accident on Vellore bypass' refers to Vellore, while the article places the accident on the Villupuram bypass; this is a location error.
